WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.230
I did it! I did it!

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.240
Now, once I get the armor to Azuchi Castle,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.980
the Date clan's long-cherished desire...

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.990
Nice job, for a hick samurai from Oushuu.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.490
Hand that over.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.110
It won't do you any good.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.250
Ieyasu-dono...

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.580
I'm going to conquer this land.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.250
And I'll start...

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.320
by killing you.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.230
<i>What a failure!</i>

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.440
<i>I wasn't able to detect her betrayal...</i>

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.770
<i>Curse you, Masamune!</i>

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.080
<i>Why did Masamune-san...</i>

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.360
<i>But Masamune-san is...</i>

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.400
<i>She's...</i>

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.320
Hide-san!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.260
<i>Why?</i>

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.700
<i>Why?!</i>

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.970
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.970
<b>Thief Maiden</b>

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.650
Hideyoshi!

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.500
Did Masamune bring her army?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.580
Ow...

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.740
I'm sorry!

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.840
Masamune-san!

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.350
What?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.610
Are you OK?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.340
Masamune-san!

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.640
Masamune!

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.100
Masamune, how dare you...

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.260
How dare you betray us?

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.260
Stop it, Akerin!

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.400
She's hurt!

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.970
Shut up and get out of the way!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.600
Mitsuhide!

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.410
My lord!

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.280
Masamune.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:49.040
If you're down there... 
How are they attacking my castle?

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.530
Hey, what's going on?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:04:02.070
I wasn't the only one after the Crimson Armor...

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:02.720
What?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.830
I'm going to kill you.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:24.800
My lord.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.170
If a cuckoo won't cry,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.400
just wait till it does.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.880
I'm glad I waited.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.440
Too easy.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.810
Hanzou.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:58.570
Right.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.390
I got as far as stealing the armor from Honnouji.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.340
Why did you try to steal the armor?

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.650
So the Date clan could conquer the land.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.750
Shut up!

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.600
We need to hurry to the castle!

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.230
I'll get that brat!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.210
Masamune-san, are you OK?

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.150
My lord.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.380
It's about time for the 
kid-general, Oda, to return.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.740
Let's go, Hanzou.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.660
Ma'am.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.710
Um... Masamune-san,

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.310
you're Date-sensei, aren't you?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:22.680
At Honnouji, you called me Hide-san.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.370
I never expected to bring you with me.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.210
What do you mean?

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:40.790
When I used this...

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.090
That was you?

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:58.030
I had planned to go back to the Warring States era,

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:00.550
to search for the Crimson Armor.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.440
But I ended up in this world instead.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.770
And you were brought with me...

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.980
I'm sure that your getting caught up

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.280
in this broke a lot of things.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:16.300
But the Crimson Armor exists in this world, too...

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.840
You wanted the Crimson Armor that much?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.580
If I get it...

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.740
Sensei!

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.730
Anyway, I should tend to your wounds.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.220
If my horse were still here...

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.550
The horse, right?

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.820
I'll find it.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.910
Please...

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.980
My lord...

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.510
It's quiet.

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:54.050
Did they fall victim to the castle's traps?

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.030
No.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:58.160
Why would the castle inhabitants 
fall silent as well?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.540
Those three leaves... That's Tokugawa's flag!

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.570
Hanzou.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:43.880
Hanzou.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:44.290
Yes.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.250
My lord...

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.040
My lord!

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.980
So that's the path?

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.580
My lord is more amazing than usual today...

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.400
So amazing, it's scary!

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.250
Hanzou!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.360
My lord! My lord!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:44.410
Hang on!

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.520
We're almost to the castle.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.730
Thank you.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:53.730
Date-sensei... Earlier, I didn't hear you.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.650
Why were you looking for the armor?

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.940
Because I am Lord Date Masamune's descendant.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.320
The dream of conquest that 
my ancestor never attained...

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.320
For generations, his descendants 
have tried to make it a reality.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:12.010
To forge Japan into what it should truly be.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.020
To make that happen, I...

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.750
Sensei!

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.290
Date-sensei!

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:40.450
Attack!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.450
Take Ieyasu's head!

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:50.570
That's...

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.030
A barrier placed by Ieyasu.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.220
My lord.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.370
I haven't been in a real battle for a while.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.670
Show them the Oda clan's power!

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:39.520
She's crazy.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.830
We don't even know if the armor's legend is true.

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.500
The armor...

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.650
Sensei?

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.090
Thank you.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:51.760
I'm all right now.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.660
The legend of the armor is true.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:59.440
But I've never heard of it.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:04.290
During the era in which you and I lived, 
the legend is still unknown.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.830
Then how did you hear about it?

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:15.400
One day, a Date clan member, 
from the distant future,

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.800
appeared before me.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:30.850
<b>You're a Date clan member. As your mother, 
I think you should live in a way that
you stop worrying over the little things. Instead, follow a path that 
will not shame your family. Why not return? 
We can discuss it.</b>

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:42.950
I screwed up...

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.820
He'd tried to travel to the Warring States period,

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:52.150
but had ended up before me.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.760
It failed then, too?

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:56.560
That aside!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.060
That's...

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:02.180
That the Date clan may conquer...

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.790
The Crimson Armor...

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:07.950
Wait!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:13.620
He appeared and then, 
just as quickly, disappeared.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.990
At first, I thought it was a dream or an illusion.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:23.380
But then, I caught a last glimpse of the data,

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.490
and I saw he'd found something,

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.990
somewhere only Date clan members would know.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.010
If it was true,

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:50.820
then what he'd discovered 
should still exist in our time.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:55.480
To find it, I returned to our 
ancestral home in Touhoku.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:14:00.020
To see if it was a dream or reality.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:05.530
If I didn't find anything, 
I planned to forget all of it.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:13.790
But when I followed my 
dim recollection of the data...

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.080
I found them.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.880
A jewel and an ancient scroll, 
just like the ones he'd had.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.560
I felt the hand of fate.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:43.070
It wasn't a coincidence that 
he'd appeared before me.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:47.020
That is how I discovered the same scroll 
as the one he'd carried.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.690
And so, I learned the legend 
of the Crimson Armor.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.090
With that armor, the Date clan could rule Japan.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.150
I could achieve what our clan's founder

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:59.010
had always desired.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:02.730
But if you did that, wouldn't history change?

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.600
Is that possible?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.320
It is.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:08.820
I wish to fix a perverted history.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:11.080
If the proper person doesn't come to rule,

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.050
a proper history is impossible.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.890
It will not be Nobunaga who rules.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:23.380
Let alone Ieyasu...

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.800
The Date clan's conquest of Japan

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.690
is history's true path.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:49.710
Hanzou.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:50.700
Ma'am.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.390
Hanzou.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.210
Ma'am.

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:06.440
Hanzou.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.140
Ma'am.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:09.350
Hanzou.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:09.970
Ma'am.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:12.470
Hanzou.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:13.280
Ma'am.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.660
All of you Hanzous, go at once!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.490
Ma'am.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:42.020
I never thought she'd get this far.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:48.710
I'll go get some stuff to patch you up, OK?

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.860
I wonder what happened to the armor...

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:56.700
Well, I don't expect Ieyasu 
to be capable of handling it.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:00.120
You haven't given up on the armor?

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:02.430
If I leave them alone,

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:05.150
either Nobunaga or Ieyasu will conquer.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:07.910
That won't change the world at all.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.390
For the world to be led in the correct direction,

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.380
I, as a Date clan member, must conquer.

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:15.930
Why do you want to do that?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.880
You're acting kind of weird, sensei.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:20.060
The armor's made you go nuts!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.520
That may be so.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:30.730
But that armor... It's worth that much.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.970
At last, this land is mine to rule.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.640
No way!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.250
What is that?

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.810
The jewel is responding to something.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.660
It couldn't be the armor!

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:12.910
That's impossible.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.750
That wasn't in the scroll.

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:15.990
Date-sensei!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:18.090
It's the armor!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.860
The armor has activated!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.130
But why?

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:24.240
Since I have the jewel right here,
it shouldn't do that!

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.080
This can't be!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.870
How is Ieyasu doing this?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.170
Sensei, is Tokunyan OK?

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:34.710
Controlling the armor's power requires this jewel.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:37.870
If she wears the armor without the jewel,

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.650
it will go out of control!

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:41.010
No way...

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:42.300
Tokunyan!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:46.650
I never told anyone about the jewel.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:48.820
I never expected that to work against me!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:54.650
Damn it.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:57.780
My lord!

00:18:58.510 --> 00:18:59.320
Hideyoshi!

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.320
My lord, save Tokunyan!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.460
Something awful is going to happen!

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:05.830
What's going on, Hideyoshi?

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.200
What's gotten into you?

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.530
Tokunyan's going to—

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.710
I made a big mistake.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:21.320
I wanted to see how far Ieyasu's magic could take her...

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.260
I didn't think she'd be able to activate it!

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.480
It will be uncontrollable!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.190
That's as far as you go, girl!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.550
You're in the way, doggy.

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.870
Shiro!

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:35.790
Shiro!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.480
Ieyasu got the armor...

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.640
Shiro?

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.080
What happened to Tokunyan?

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.050
Hey!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.370
Masamune!

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.800
What are you doing here?

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:51.310
The armor has activated.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.460
What?

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:58.210
One who wears the Crimson Armor 
with evil in their soul

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:01.240
gains power to destroy the land.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.850
That is what the scroll said.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:05.110
Ieyasu is...

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.370
By activating the armor,

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:11.800
she has awakened the 
evil heart hidden within it...

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:13.870
No...

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.820
What will happen to Tokunyan?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:52.490
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:27.050
Time for a three-round fight!

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:27.830
Start!

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.860
Hit it, wear it, rock-paper-scissors!

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:31.930
<b>Round One</b>

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:32.930
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:32.970
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:32.580
Hit it, wear it, rock-paper-scissors!

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:33.570
It was a tie!

00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:35.950
Yes! I did it!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:38.090
That sucks.

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:40.060
You're such a kid.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:43.150
What are you talking about, sensei?

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:45.920
Okay, time for the next one!

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:47.260
<b>Round Two</b>

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:45.900
Rock-paper-scissors, shoot!

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.350
Okay, let's go.

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:47.350
Right.

00:23:47.350 --> 00:23:49.040
Rock comes first. Rock-paper-scissors.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:50.040
Look over... There!

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:51.340
Rock comes first. Rock-paper-scissors.

00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:52.080
Look over... There!

00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:52.490
Rock comes—

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:54.620
Make sure you watch next time!

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:56.580
Preview

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:56.580
Battle Maiden
